From: Graft64 contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: include cstdarg for CRT variadic functions

IO.cpp uses va_start, va_arg and va_end. Include their defining header
explicitly for LLVM-MinGW 20260826 rather than relying on transitive includes.
Authored locally from the native ARM64 CI failure against locked FEX-2607;
no code or patch was copied from another project. No runtime logic changes.

Upstream-Status: Pending (not submitted)

diff --git a/Source/Windows/Common/CRT/IO.cpp b/Source/Windows/Common/CRT/IO.cpp
--- a/Source/Windows/Common/CRT/IO.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/Common/CRT/IO.cpp
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <algorithm>
 #include <cstdlib>
 #include <cstdio>
+#include <cstdarg>
 #include <cstdint>
 #include <cerrno>
 #include <io.h>
